{"term":"compress","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:50d2447d6b47ddf4a5","definition":"To make smaller; to press or squeeze together, or to make something occupy a smaller space or volume.","example":"The force required to compress a spring varies linearly with the displacement.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["compact","condense","pack","press","squash","squeeze"],"antonyms":["expand"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["compressed","compressed air","compressedly","compressibility","compressible","compressingly","compression","compressive","compressive strength","compressor","compressure","decompress","overcompress","precompress","recompress","supercompress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0ab5a5d1ad148a6e38","definition":"To be pressed together or folded by compression into a more economic, easier format.","example":"Our new model compresses easily, ideal for storage and travel","pos":"verb","synonyms":["contract"],"antonyms":["decontract"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["compressed","compressed air","compressedly","compressibility","compressible","compressingly","compression","compressive","compressive strength","compressor","compressure","decompress","overcompress","precompress","recompress","supercompress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ab97948d84d4d88a76","definition":"To condense into a more economic, easier format.","example":"This chart compresses the entire audit report into a few lines on a single diagram.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["astringe","compact","telescope","compactify","condense","densitize","pack","press","mash","scrunch","smush","squoosh","squash","squish","squeeze","thring","thrutch"],"antonyms":["decompact","decompactify","decompress","expand","uncompress","densen"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["compressed","compressed air","compressedly","compressibility","compressible","compressingly","compression","compressive","compressive strength","compressor","compressure","decompress","overcompress","precompress","recompress","supercompress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6d95ac05adee8f1aa2","definition":"To abridge.","example":"If you try to compress the entire book into a three-sentence summary, you will lose a lot of information.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["abridge","condense","shorten","truncate","abbreviate","abridge","chop down","chop off","cut short","compress","condense","curt","curtail","lop off","make shorter","pare","prune","reduce in length","shorten","trim","truncate","saw off"],"antonyms":["expand","lengthen"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["compressed","compressed air","compressedly","compressibility","compressible","compressingly","compression","compressive","compressive strength","compressor","compressure","decompress","overcompress","precompress","recompress","supercompress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b24f8c02faf5967737","definition":"To make digital information smaller by encoding it using fewer bits.","example":"The command-line tool gzip allows you to compress files in a few different ways. First, gzip can compress results from standard input.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["zip"],"antonyms":["uncompress","decompress","unzip"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["compressed","compressed air","compressedly","compressibility","compressible","compressingly","compression","compressive","compressive strength","compressor","compressure","decompress","overcompress","precompress","recompress","supercompress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ddee41925763a90e4c","definition":"To make a pulse or particle bunch shorter by applying dispersion to it.","example":"Diffraction gratings are by far the most common elements used to stretch and compress pulses because of their substantial angular dispersion, […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["astringe","compact","telescope","compactify","condense","densitize","pack","press","mash","scrunch","smush","squoosh","squash","squish","squeeze","thring","thrutch"],"antonyms":["stretch"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["compressed","compressed air","compressedly","compressibility","compressible","compressingly","compression","compressive","compressive strength","compressor","compressure","decompress","overcompress","precompress","recompress","supercompress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/compress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:df206e158b99a2565a","definition":"To embrace sexually.","example":"This nymph compreſs'd by him vvho rules the day, / VVhom Delphi and the Delian iſle obey, / Andræmon lov'd; and, bleſs'd in all thoſe charms / That pleas'd a God, ſucceeded to her arms.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["astringe","compact","telescope","compactify","condense","densitize","pack","press","mash","scrunch","smush","squoosh","squash","squish","squeeze","thring","thrutch"],"antonyms":["decompact","decompactify","decompress","expand","uncompress","densen"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["c